Fix type confusion and out-of-bounds reference indices while
unserializing bytecode.

ReadBCLang() reads the type after BCREPDEF from the stream and passes
it to allocSExp().  A malformed type can create a cons cell labelled
as a vector, so the next garbage collection follows invalid pointers.
The indices used by BCREPREF and BCREPDEF also reach the reps vector
without bounds checks.  Validate both indices and accept only LANGSXP
or LISTSXP, including their attribute variants, for a definition.

Found by OSS-Fuzz's unserialize target (testcase 5865026871951360).
The issue also reproduces in released R 4.6.1.

Upstream status: proposed in r-devel/r-svn PR #348.  Its regression
test in tests/reg-tests-1b.R is left out here so this carry patch does
not go stale with that file.  Delete the patch after the fix lands in
R trunk.

diff --git a/src/main/serialize.c b/src/main/serialize.c
index e5e749a79c..d601881ca5 100644
--- a/src/main/serialize.c
+++ b/src/main/serialize.c
@@ -2144,7 +2144,12 @@ static SEXP ReadBCLang(int type, SEXP ref_table, SEXP reps,
 {
     switch (type) {
     case BCREPREF:
-	return VECTOR_ELT(reps, InInteger(stream));
+	{
+	    int pos = InInteger(stream);
+	    if (pos < 0 || pos >= LENGTH(reps))
+		error(_("bytecode reference index out of range"));
+	    return VECTOR_ELT(reps, pos);
+	}
     case BCREPDEF:
     case LANGSXP:
     case LISTSXP:
@@ -2156,12 +2161,18 @@ static SEXP ReadBCLang(int type, SEXP ref_table, SEXP reps,
 	    int hasattr = false;
 	    if (type == BCREPDEF) {
 		pos = InInteger(stream);
+		if (pos < 0 || pos >= LENGTH(reps))
+		    error(_("bytecode reference index out of range"));
 		type = InInteger(stream);
 	    }
 	    switch (type) {
 	    case ATTRLANGSXP: type = LANGSXP; hasattr = TRUE; break;
 	    case ATTRLISTSXP: type = LISTSXP; hasattr = TRUE; break;
 	    }
+	    /* the BCREPDEF type comes from the stream; allocSExp would
+	       happily build a cons cell labelled as any other type */
+	    if (type != LANGSXP && type != LISTSXP)
+		error(_("ReadBCLang: invalid type %i"), type);
 	    PROTECT(ans = allocSExp(type));
 	    if (pos >= 0)
 		SET_VECTOR_ELT(reps, pos, ans);
